# Vacation requests — for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Start the API (`npm run dev` in backend/), then send the two logins first.
# Dates are relative to today ({{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 30 d}} = today + 30 days),
# so the file never goes stale. Run it top to bottom; sending "create" twice hits the overlap
# rule (409), which is expected — cancel it or pick other dates.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8888
@password = Password123!
@requesterToken = {{loginRequester.response.body.token}}
@validatorToken = {{loginValidator.response.body.token}}
@requestId = {{createRequest.response.body.id}}

### Login as a requester (Alice)
# @name loginRequester
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Login as the validator
# @name loginValidator
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "validator@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }


### ================= Requester =================

### Submit a request (201, Pending) — the requests below act on it
# @name createRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{
  "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 120 d}}",
  "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 125 d}}",
  "reason": "Ski trip"
}

### My requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

### Change dates/reason of my Pending request
PUT {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{
  "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 121 d}}",
  "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 126 d}}",
  "reason": "Ski trip, one day later"
}

### Create a throwaway request, to cancel it below
# @name createToCancel
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{ "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 250 d}}", "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 252 d}}" }

### Cancel it (204) — only Pending requests can be cancelled
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{createToCancel.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}


### A second request, for the validator to reject
# @name createToReject
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{ "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 160 d}}", "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 163 d}}" }


### ================= Validator =================

### All requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### Filter by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests?status=Pending
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### Pagination: second page of 5 (the response has total and totalPages)
GET {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests?status=Pending&page=2&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### One request, with its user
GET {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{requestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### Filter by user (Alice)
GET {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests?userId={{loginRequester.response.body.user.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### Requesters, for the "filter by user" list
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=Requester
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### Approve the first request
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{requestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

### Reject the second one — a comment is required
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{createToReject.response.body.id}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

{ "comment": "Release week, please pick other dates." }


### ================= Both roles =================

### Team planning: Approved + Pending vacations, next 90 days by default
GET {{baseUrl}}/team/vacations
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

### Team planning for a chosen window
GET {{baseUrl}}/team/vacations?from={{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD"}}&to={{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 180 d}}
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}


### ================= Business rules (expected errors) =================

### Rule 1 — 400: end date must be after start date
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{ "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 300 d}}", "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 300 d}}" }

### Rule 2 — 409: overlaps the request created above
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{ "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 123 d}}", "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 130 d}}" }

### Rule 3 — 409 after the request was approved or rejected: it can no longer be changed
PUT {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{requestId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{ "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 121 d}}", "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 127 d}}" }

### Rule 4 — 400: cannot start in the past
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}

{ "startDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" -3 d}}", "endDate": "{{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD" 2 d}}" }

### Rule 5 — 400: rejecting needs a comment
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{requestId}}/reject
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{validatorToken}}

{ "comment": "" }

### Rule 6 — 403: a requester cannot approve
POST {{baseUrl}}/vacation-requests/{{requestId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{requesterToken}}
